{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>I have much.</b> He spoke with pride and arrogance of heart. And if you look at the verses you will find that Jacob speaks at length with him while he is terse, and this itself indicates his pride and haughtiness. Besides which, you will find in Jacob that he mentioned HaShem in all his words, saying ״הילדים אשר חנן אלהים את עבדך״, ״כראות פני אלהים״, ״כי חנני אלהים״ — but you will not find in Esav that he mentioned HaShem at all." "<b>My brother, let what is yours be yours.</b> They interpreted in Bereshit Rabbah: until now the blessings were in doubt in his hand, but now they were confirmed in his hand, as it says: ״אחי יהי לך אשר לך״. And there are here ten letters, corresponding to the ten blessings in the blessing of ויתן לך. If so, then the blessings were fulfilled for him from the mouth of his father and from the mouth of Esav, and also from his angel."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:23.947860605Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}